  "summary": "Three November 2026 preprints refine interface-sensitive optical and thermal probes, from SHG modelling to cross-technique thermometry of monolayer TMDs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the resolution of interfacial properties using optical and thermal probes. The preprint arXiv:2611.25746 applies angle- and polarisation-resolved second-harmonic generation to separate surface, bulk and buried-interface contributions in Ta2O5 thin films. The preprint arXiv:2611.30448 examines the formal basis of surface SHG modelling and reports that transfer matrix and multiple reflection formalisms agree only under specific interface implementations, which is relevant to how such contributions are extracted. The preprint arXiv:2611.26129 addresses a different interfacial quantity, thermal boundary conductance in four monolayer TMDs on sapphire, by benchmarking Raman thermometry, SThM and FDTR against one another. The new elements are the explicit separation of buried-interface contributions and the systematic cross-technique comparison of interfacial thermal transport. The items do not establish a shared measurement platform, and the TMD thermal study is methodologically distinct from the SHG work.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
